[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 1"""
 date="2026-10-07T18:12:17Z"
 content="""
What's weird about your situation and I don't understand is you do not have
a remotes/hub-con/git-annex, which would be the usual name of the remote
tracking branch that git-annex would normally automatically merge. 

You do have a local branch named hub-con/git-annex. I don't understand
where that came from. Maybe that ought to be merged and isn't being merged,
but you're clearly doing something unusual to have that rather than the
regular remote tracking branch.

Anyway, to dispell some of the other confusion in this bug report:

`git-annex push` does not treat a failure to push the git-annex branch as
an error since it has already sent the same information to the remote
in a successful force-push of the synced/git-annex branch. So that is all a
red herring.

And when you ran "git annex merge hub-con", that is the wrong command to 
merge the git-annex branch from the remote. That command
merges a branch named "hub-con" into the current branch.
"""]]
